(version 1)

# nice!view reversible display mount
#
# The 5 display holes are NON-PLATED on purpose. A pin is soldered to the
# display, passed through the bare hole, and soldered to ONE face of the
# board. Because the barrel is unplated, the F.Cu ring and the B.Cu ring
# around the same hole are electrically independent -- that isolation is what
# lets the front-side jumpers pick the pin mapping while the display itself is
# soldered from the back.
#
# KiCad reports copper concentric with an NPTH as a hole-clearance error. Here
# the concentricity IS the design. Waived for this footprint only; the
# condition names both A and B so it also covers a routed track arriving at a
# ring. Verified: substituting a non-existent reference into the same
# condition waives nothing, so the exception cannot leak board-wide.
#
# The matching solder-mask exception is NOT here -- it lives on the footprint
# itself as (attr ... allow_soldermask_bridges), which is tighter than a rule.

(rule "niceview_npth_ring_hole_clearance"
	(constraint hole_clearance (min 0mm))
	(condition "A.memberOfFootprint('display*') || B.memberOfFootprint('display*')"))

# Per-switch diode nests INSIDE the switch courtyard
#
# The PG1316S has a pocket in its body for the LED/diode. Chalk puts the SOD-123
# there at switch-local (0, -2.700) -- measured across all 21 of its diodes,
# stdev 0.0000 -- and the datasheet LAND PATTERN RECOMMENDATION shows the pocket
# on the opposite half of the body from the two terminals (ours at y = +2.650).
#
# So the diode courtyard is SUPPOSED to sit inside the switch courtyard. KiCad
# calls that 42 courtyard overlaps; here it is the intended assembly. The diode
# lies under the switch body, not beside it.
#
# Scoped to diode references only. Verified: the same rule with a non-existent
# reference ('NOPE*') waives nothing (42 overlaps remain), so this cannot leak
# board-wide and silently hide a real collision between other parts.

(rule "diode_nests_inside_switch_courtyard"
	(constraint courtyard_clearance (min -2mm))
	(condition "A.Reference == 'D*' || B.Reference == 'D*'"))

# Battery pads 28/29 on the XIAO: front and back stack on the same two holes
#
# Pads 28 and 29 (BAT+ / BAT-) are through-hole so the connection can cross the
# board: the pads sit on the UNDERSIDE of the XIAO, so the module is soldered
# from the opposite face. Mirroring the footprint swaps 28<->29, so each hole is
# VCC for one mount side and GND for the other -- which is what the VCC/GND
# solder jumpers select. Only one XIAO is ever populated.
#
# KiCad sees the front footprint's pad 28 and the back footprint's pad 29
# occupying one hole with different pad numbers and reports clearance 0 and a
# mask bridge. Both are the intended geometry. Scoped to REF**, which belongs
# only to the two XIAO footprints, AND to pad numbers 28/29, so no other pad on
# the module is covered.
#
# Verified: 'A.Footprint_Name == XIAO*' waives nothing (count stays 14), while
# this condition drops it to 10 -- i.e. exactly the 4 battery-pad pairs.

(rule "xiao_battery_pads_share_holes"
	(constraint clearance (min 0mm))
	(condition "(A.memberOfFootprint('REF**') && B.memberOfFootprint('REF**')) && (A.Pad_Number == '28' || A.Pad_Number == '29') && (B.Pad_Number == '28' || B.Pad_Number == '29')"))

(rule "xiao_battery_pads_share_hole_clearance"
	(constraint hole_clearance (min 0mm))
	(condition "(A.memberOfFootprint('REF**') && B.memberOfFootprint('REF**')) && (A.Pad_Number == '28' || A.Pad_Number == '29') && (B.Pad_Number == '28' || B.Pad_Number == '29')"))
